## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design crash‑safe, low‑level memory allocators for persistent memory, including ordering, recovery, and reclamation. Tests understanding of write amplification, ABA risks, and practical recovery semantics.

## Key Concepts

- Persistent memory semantics and durability guarantees
- Log-structured allocation and per-block headers
- Versioning, CRC, and bitmap for consistency
- Recovery: replay log up to last committed epoch; handle partial writes
- Cache-line padding and memory fences to avoid false sharing and ABA

